// The Clang module of the braille translation's interface (DR34),
// ../TextMouthBrailleLibrary.h, which only the iPhone's code imports
// (BrailleTranslator, under #if os(iOS)): the iPhone app links the library
// (TextMouthBrailleLibrary_iOS and liblouis_iOS in project.yml) and calls it in
// its own process, while the Mac app links neither, since its helper program
// runs the same code.
//
// It has a map of its own, in a folder named after the module, where Clang
// looks for it on the include path the apps already search
// (TextMouthBraille/include), so that ../module.modulemap, from which the
// braille protocol's module is built, is left as it was: GitHub's runners keep
// the modules built from that map and its header between runs, and a change to
// either fails the next build with a stale module ("has been modified since
// the module file").
module TextMouthBrailleLibrary {
    header "../TextMouthBrailleLibrary.h"
    export *
}
